      "decision_index": 47,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "GPT5n Stoic chose to hardcast Fury for {3}{R}{R} when they only have a single Mountain on the battlefield and no way to produce 5 mana this turn. Even with City of Traitors in hand (which they could play for {C}{C} + Mountain for {R} = 3 mana total), they still can't reach {3}{R}{R}. Meanwhile, they have Broadside Bombardiers (a red card) in hand that could be exiled to pay Fury's Evoke cost, allowing them to immediately deal 4 damage to the opponent's Otter Token and potentially Stormchaser's Talent-related threats. The Evoke line clears the board immediately for free, while hardcasting is either illegal or requires waiting multiple turns during which the opponent's board grows. Even if they could eventually hardcast, Fury would just die to the opponent's removal given the cards in the graveyard (Lightning Bolt, etc.). The Evoke line is clearly superior - trade a Broadside Bombardiers (mediocre in this matchup without board presence) to kill the opponent's creatures now.",
      "action_taken": "Chose to hardcast Fury for {3}{R}{R} instead of using Evoke",
      "better_line": "Cast Fury with Evoke by exiling Broadside Bombardiers (a red card) from hand to immediately deal 4 damage divided among the Otter Token and any other targets, clearing the opponent's board pressure",
