      "decision_index": 57,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "With City of Traitors in hand and only one Mountain on the battlefield, playing City of Traitors would provide 3 mana (1 Mountain + 2 from City) enabling a turn 4 Blood Moon, which would be devastating against the opponent who relies on Volcanic Islands and Misty Rainforest as their mana base - turning all their nonbasics into Mountains and cutting them off blue mana entirely. The opponent has Stormchaser's Talent and an Otter token applying pressure, and their graveyard is stocked for potential Mystic Sanctuary or recursion plays. Blood Moon would lock them out of the game. Instead, playing Urza's Saga is slow - it won't make a creature token until next turn (chapter II) and won't search until the turn after that (chapter III), by which time the opponent can continue developing. Urza's Saga also gets destroyed by the Blood Moon the player wants to eventually cast.",
